"build:tokens":{"site":"build","slug":"tokens","title":"Tokens: how AI reads text","url":"https://build.amaete.com/tokens/","blurb":"Watch a tokenizer chop sentences into pieces on a conveyor.","checks":[{"q":"What does a tokenizer do?","a":["Translates text","Cuts text into numbered pieces the model can read","Checks spelling"],"ok":1,"why":"It turns text into a list of token numbers. The model only ever sees those numbers."},{"q":"How does byte pair encoding learn its tokens?","a":["From a dictionary","By merging the most common pair of pieces, again and again","At random"],"ok":1,"why":"It counts neighbouring pairs in its training text and merges the most common one, many times over."},{"q":"Why does Yoruba need more tokens here?","a":["Yoruba is a longer language","The tokenizer learned its pieces from English text","Tone marks are ignored"],"ok":1,"why":"Pieces come from the training text. Text it rarely saw gets cut into small, many pieces."}]},
